-- title:
--   Unique minimal prime over π₀ in the j-finite chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element whose image lies in $A$; write $A_0$ for the contraction $A\cap k_0$, and assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, that it is henselian, that its residue field is algebraically closed, and that every element of $A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Let $\ell'$ be a prime with $\ell'\neq q$, $\ell'\ge 3$ and $\ell'\nmid M'$, and let $\xi\in k_0$ be a primitive $q\ell'$-th root of unity admitting a ring embedding $\iota\colon k_0\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. Let $K''$ be an intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)/k_0$ equal to `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. the $k_0$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb Q$-rational $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $\ell'^2M'$ for the subgroup $H$ of $(\mathbb Z/\ell'^2M')^\times$ that is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell')^\times$, together with algebra and scalar-tower data making $K''$ an $A_0$-algebra over $k_0$. Let $j''\in K''$ be nonzero with underlying Laurent series the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{power series } j_{\mathrm{Num}})$ of $j$. Then, in the $A_0$-subalgebra $C''=$ `chartAlgFin` $A_0\,K''\,j''$ of $K''$ attached to the singleton $\{j''\}$, every minimal prime $P$ over the ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$ is contained in every prime ideal $\mathfrak y$ of $C''$ containing that image.
--
--   This is the irreducibility of the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart of the integral model at level $\ell'^2M'$ prime to the residue characteristic $q$: the ideal generated by the uniformiser has a unique minimal prime, which is the smallest prime containing $\pi_0$, reflecting good reduction of the modular curve at $q$. It is used in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin).
